docs/backlog.md:111:**D144 — DEVDESK-328 (S-03b): the path trace has a fifth tab, Path, in the network view. Decided: (1) Path is the fifth tab, last. (2) Streaming is a callback of the engine, `nettrace.TraceEach(ctx, target, opts, onHop)`, not a field of `Options`, which stays comparable (`Trace` calls it with nil). The engine may report a hop above the terminal one, so the UI reconciles with `Result.Hops` at done. (3) The target field takes `host` or `host:port`: the port is validated and shown in the header, but has no effect on the probes, which stay UDP to port 33435 (option A). (4) `H` (`keymap.Diagnose`) on the Local route row of Diagnostics opens Path prefilled with the host only, and never launches; `enter` launches, `esc` cancels. (5) Error labels are fixed texts; the system error text goes to the log only. The body is always the hop table; the target sits in the bar slot. Hypotheses (prudent defaults, not validated): 30 hops, 3 s per probe and 30 s overall (engine defaults); the first IPv4 address when a name resolves to several; `enter` greyed outside supported Linux and refused with a Warn. Why: the plan `.claude/plans/devdesk-328-path-tab-plan.md` (main checkout) keeps `Options` comparable and gives the view a single streamed source; `H` prefills without sending, since nothing leaves before an explicit `enter`. No ADR: local and reversible. **Plane:** DEVDESK-328 (S-03b), dated 2026-11-14. Sources: the plan above, D143, worktree `.worktrees/feat/devdesk-328-path-tab` (uncommitted when this entry was written).**
docs/backlog.md:115:**D142 — DEVDESK-410 (security): `internal/oci` no longer sends registry credentials or follows a link off the origin they were meant for, and bounds the token response. Three pre-existing weaknesses found by the security review of DEVDESK-306 (D135) are fixed: (1) the `Link: rel="next"` of the tag list is no longer followed off-origin (`sameOrigin`); a foreign `next` is an error wrapping the sentinel `ErrTagsNextOffOrigin` (`errors.Is`, destination host only), with no partial list, because a short list could give `imageupdate` and the security remediation a false "up to date" (the catalog walker keeps `truncated=true` with the names already read); (2) `registryHTTPClient` has a `CheckRedirect` (`refuseOffOriginRedirect`) that refuses any redirect leaving the origin of the first request (scheme, host and port, compared against `via[0]`), instead of following it without `Authorization`. The choice: an explicit error is safer than a silent anonymous retry; the error is `refusing redirect to another origin (host)`, wraps `errOffOriginRedirect`, and carries no target path or query (a signed URL reaches neither footer nor logs). Consequence: a registry that redirects to another host is unusable with this client, and some redirects once followed are now refused (http to https on the same host, `host` to `host:443`, a different host case: exact scheme and host:port, refused when in doubt); (3) the Bearer token endpoint's response is capped at 1 MiB (`maxTokenResponse`), and a larger body is an error, not a silent cut. Residual risks found and not fixed: a Bearer `realm` in `http://` announced by an https registry sends the Basic credentials in clear (initial request, outside this fix); and `registry.go` puts the raw request URL in the error prefix, so a userinfo in `apiURL` would appear there (pre-existing). Found and not fixed, out of scope: `internal/oci/oci.go:46` (`http.Client` with neither `CheckRedirect` nor timeout, registry credentials), `internal/registrymgr/nexus.go:212` (Basic auth, redirects followed, unbounded `ReadAll`), `internal/ui/oci_resources/commands.go:412` (unbounded `ReadAll`, no credentials): to be handled in a follow-up story if the user creates one. No ADR: local and reversible. **Plane:** DEVDESK-410, dated 2026-11-14. Sources: the Plane story (no plan file), `docs/architecture/network.md`, D135, worktree `.worktrees/fix/devdesk-410-registry-credential-origin` (uncommitted when this entry was written).**
