docs/backlog.md:115:**D142 — DEVDESK-410 (security): `internal/oci` no longer sends registry credentials or follows a link off the origin they were meant for, and bounds the token response. Three pre-existing weaknesses found by the security review of DEVDESK-306 (D135) are fixed: (1) the `Link: rel="next"` of the tag list is no longer followed off-origin (`sameOrigin`); a foreign `next` is an error wrapping the sentinel `ErrTagsNextOffOrigin` (`errors.Is`, destination host only), with no partial list, because a short list could give `imageupdate` and the security remediation a false "up to date" (the catalog walker keeps `truncated=true` with the names already read); (2) `registryHTTPClient` has a `CheckRedirect` (`refuseOffOriginRedirect`) that refuses any redirect leaving the origin of the first request (scheme, host and port, compared against `via[0]`), instead of following it without `Authorization`. The choice: an explicit error is safer than a silent anonymous retry; the error is `refusing redirect to another origin (host)`, wraps `errOffOriginRedirect`, and carries no target path or query (a signed URL reaches neither footer nor logs). Consequence: a registry that redirects to another host is unusable with this client, and some redirects once followed are now refused (http to https on the same host, `host` to `host:443`, a different host case: exact scheme and host:port, refused when in doubt); (3) the Bearer token endpoint's response is capped at 1 MiB (`maxTokenResponse`), and a larger body is an error, not a silent cut. Residual risks found and not fixed: a Bearer `realm` in `http://` announced by an https registry sends the Basic credentials in clear (initial request, outside this fix); and `registry.go` puts the raw request URL in the error prefix, so a userinfo in `apiURL` would appear there (pre-existing). Found and not fixed, out of scope: `internal/oci/oci.go:46` (`http.Client` with neither `CheckRedirect` nor timeout, registry credentials), `intern